1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,720
In the summer of 1944,

2
00:00:02,150 --> 00:00:04,340
two Frenchmen on bicycles stopped in shock.

3
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,890
Four American soldiers had just picked up

4
00:00:06,890 --> 00:00:07,740
a Sherman tank.

5
00:00:08,068 --> 00:00:10,238
The Sherman was America's main battle tank:

6
00:00:10,748 --> 00:00:11,738
33 tons of steel.

7
00:00:12,017 --> 00:00:14,377
One soldier reportedly shrugged: "Americans

8
00:00:14,377 --> 00:00:15,367
are very strong."

9
00:00:15,773 --> 00:00:17,283
The truth? The tank was rubber.

10
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:18,903
And it weighed 93 pounds.

11
00:00:19,335 --> 00:00:21,295
It belonged to one of the most secret units

12
00:00:21,295 --> 00:00:24,115
of World War II: the 23rd Headquarters Special

13
00:00:24,115 --> 00:00:25,865
Troops. The Ghost Army.

14
00:00:26,158 --> 00:00:28,228
1,100 men, many of them artists,

15
00:00:28,538 --> 00:00:31,028
designers and ad men from New York and Philadelphia.

16
00:00:31,738 --> 00:00:33,538
Their mission: make the Germans believe

17
00:00:33,538 --> 00:00:35,042
they were 30,000.

18
00:00:35,107 --> 00:00:36,827
German intelligence watched the front three

19
00:00:36,827 --> 00:00:38,007
ways: from the air,

20
00:00:38,007 --> 00:00:39,677
over the radio, and through spies.

21
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:41,937
The Ghost Army faked all three.

22
00:00:42,228 --> 00:00:43,918
From the air: inflatable tanks,

23
00:00:44,068 --> 00:00:45,878
trucks and artillery, set up overnight.

24
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:48,028
A bulldozer cut fake tank tracks,

25
00:00:48,028 --> 00:00:50,088
so the scene looked real in reconnaissance

26
00:00:50,088 --> 00:00:50,578
photos.

27
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:53,413
Over the radio: operators copied the traffic

28
00:00:53,413 --> 00:00:55,753
of real divisions, down to each operator's

29
00:00:55,753 --> 00:00:57,203
style in Morse code.

30
00:00:57,472 --> 00:00:59,532
And on the ground: speakers on half-tracks

31
00:00:59,532 --> 00:01:01,172
played recordings of tank columns,

32
00:01:01,172 --> 00:01:03,102
heard up to 15 miles away.

33
00:01:04,092 --> 00:01:06,012
Soldiers wore fake unit patches and talked

34
00:01:06,012 --> 00:01:08,562
loosely in cafés where spies might be listening.

35
00:01:08,887 --> 00:01:10,277
From Normandy to the Rhine,

36
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:12,037
they staged more than twenty deceptions.

37
00:01:12,451 --> 00:01:14,721
Their biggest came in March 1945.

38
00:01:15,631 --> 00:01:17,371
To cover the Ninth Army's crossing of the

39
00:01:17,371 --> 00:01:19,951
Rhine, they faked two entire infantry divisions

40
00:01:19,951 --> 00:01:22,601
with more than 600 inflatable dummies.

41
00:01:22,931 --> 00:01:24,201
The Germans took the bait.

42
00:01:24,511 --> 00:01:25,751
The real crossing, to the north,

43
00:01:25,751 --> 00:01:26,841
met little resistance.

44
00:01:27,468 --> 00:01:29,548
The Army kept it all classified for more

45
00:01:29,548 --> 00:01:31,718
than fifty years, until 1996.

46
00:01:32,463 --> 00:01:35,223
In 2022, Congress awarded the Ghost Army

47
00:01:35,223 --> 00:01:36,543
the Congressional Gold Medal,

48
00:01:36,543 --> 00:01:38,113
for fighting with rubber,

49
00:01:38,343 --> 00:01:39,533
sound and imagination.

50
00:01:40,037 --> 00:01:41,467
Would you have fallen for it?

